   "en": {
    "headline": "Sam Altman says he wants 'tons of memory' for everyone after criticizing local AI on PCs",
    "summary_short": "Sam Altman said in an interview that it is 'terrible' to have RAM, a scarce resource, sitting idle in people's computers. After the backlash, he says he was taken out of context and wants more memory to be made.",
    "summary_long": "In an interview, the OpenAI CEO talked about people who want to run open models on their own computer (local inference). He said that, from a global perspective, it is 'pretty terrible' for everyone to have RAM, a limited resource, sitting in their computer and used 5 % of the time. Many read it as a self-serving defense of cloud AI, which is what OpenAI sells.\n\nAltman responded on X on election night. He changed his name to 'Ram Altman' and wrote that he wants people to put as much memory as they want in their computers. He added that it is annoying to be taken out of context and that he has long argued for ramping up memory production. His critics, such as the creator midudev, maintain that his words did refer to personal computers, not servers.",
    "unconfirmed_claims": []
   },
